# Branch, commit, pull request

- Never commit on `main` or `v*`. If work is on local `main`, move it to
  `<type>/<short-kebab>` first (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, …).
- Forbidden branch prefixes: `cursor/`, `claude/`, `codex/`, `agent/`, `bot/`.
- Uncommitted files and local-only commits belong on that branch, then push,
  then a pull request. Do not leave reviewable work sitting only on local `main`.
- This repo overrides a harness HEREDOC that appends footers. Write the
  message to a file. `git commit-tree` is acceptable when it stops a harness
  from appending a promotional footer. It is not a way to hide a legitimate
  trailer the authorship transition says to preserve.
- After every commit: `git log -1 --format=%B`. Record the result.
  `scripts/commit-policy.mjs` still rejects `Co-authored-by` and promotional
  `Generated with` / `Made with` / `Generated by` lines. Do not bypass the hook.
  The intended authorship policy, which is not fully active, is
  `.cursor/rules/no-co-authored-by.mdc`.
- Pull request title and body describe the change. Do not add a promotional
  tool footer. Do not fabricate a co-author.

Canon: `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/governance/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md`,
`.cursor/rules/no-co-authored-by.mdc`.
